# The gate list: one line per gate, `name|command`, run in this order by `sh scripts/run-gates.sh`. Copy it to scripts/gates.list.
# Every check goes here (the runner fails when a scripts/check-*.sh is missing from it), the catalogue docs/checks.md is
# generated from it, and nothing else names a gate. Never cut a gate to make a run faster: tag it `slow` and use --fast.
#
# A check script is described by its own header. A plain command is described by the comment lines directly above it.
# Tags after the name: `slow` (left out by --fast) and `reuse:PATH,PATH` (a PASS is stored per hash of those paths).
# group: Documentation
check-history-comments|sh scripts/check-history-comments.sh
check-comment-refs|sh scripts/check-comment-refs.sh
check-doc-links|sh scripts/check-doc-links.sh
check-docs-catalogue|sh scripts/check-docs-catalogue.sh
check-backlog-index|sh scripts/check-backlog-index.sh
check-placeholders|sh scripts/check-placeholders.sh
check-doc-map|sh scripts/check-doc-map.sh
check-dated-headings|sh scripts/check-dated-headings.sh
